  "caption": "Quinn found bouldering, loved tiny holds, then felt a pop in the ring finger. Now even holding a coffee is a struggle.\n\nFinger pulleys are bands that keep the tendons close to the bone, and crimping on small holds loads them the most. A pop can happen with milder sprains too, so it isn't automatically the worst case.\n\nWhat often helps: keep the finger gently moving while skipping crimps, climb less rather than stopping, try H-taping for light sessions, rebuild grip strength with controlled open-hand work, and return on easy grades and big holds. Hard crimping comes back last.\n\nVisible bowstringing, marked swelling or a finger that won't bend are worth getting assessed promptly.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
